  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "0.8 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 76,655 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Mixed web/news vocabulary added",
   "text": "58,434 of the reference words come from a mixed web/news corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, afr_mixed_2019_1M, 20.3 million words); 18,221 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words (922 probable English words were removed). Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  }
